rushing to catch the last trains before  the Lunar New Year many of these  passengers of the Beijing west railway  station are thinking of the coronavirus  don't think this virus has been properly  controlled I just came back to China I  read a lot of news Internet I'm not very  satisfied with how the government  prevented and controlled the disease I'm  very afraid of getting infected I am  really afraid of those people who lived  in left 400 but I do hope the situation  in Wuhan can be improved so much and  those inside the city of Wuhan are  becoming more frustrated because medical  supplies are running short and hospitals  are short-staffed many festivals for the  Lunar New Year holiday have been  cancelled across China and not just in  the central Hubei Province the epicenter  of the virus the government has closed  the Forbidden City here in Beijing over  health concerns related to the corona  virus something they didn't do some 17  years ago during the SARS crisis the  Chinese government was criticized for  the way it handled the SARS virus back  in 2003 mainly for its lack of  transparency the World Health  Organization has decided not to declare  the current outbreak a global health  emergency  but there's growing concern over the  coming week when the millions of people  who have travelled for the holiday  returned again raising the risk the  virus may be spread further by people  who are contaminated but have yet to  show symptoms  Scott Hodler al-jazeera Beijing
 

